<div class="tabpanel" role="tabpanel" id="tab-eli5" data-tab-key="eli5" data-tab-kind="eli5" aria-labelledby="tabbtn-eli5" tabindex="0">
<h2 class="panel-title">ELI5</h2>
<section id="sec-eli5-53f4137e" data-section-id="sec-eli5-53f4137e" data-origin="generated" data-eli5-actionable="true" aria-labelledby="sec-eli5-53f4137e-h">
<h2 id="sec-eli5-53f4137e-h">Guessing how many to make</h2>
<aside class="analogy"><p class="analogy-label">Think of it like</p><p>It is like buying snacks for a party when you do not know exactly how many friends will come.</p></aside>
<p>Example Widgets Inc. has to guess how many widgets people will buy before they buy them.</p>
</section>
<section id="sec-eli5-124693ce" data-section-id="sec-eli5-124693ce" data-origin="generated" data-eli5-actionable="true" aria-labelledby="sec-eli5-124693ce-h">
<h2 id="sec-eli5-124693ce-h">Keeping a few extra</h2>
<p>A small pile of extra widgets means nobody leaves empty-handed, but extras cost money to store.</p>
<aside class="callout callout--note"><p class="callout-label">Note</p><p>More online shoppers means a bigger pile is needed.</p></aside>
</section>
